FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied (meant for upstream once the namespace policy for exec entropy is settled):
- Add `redox_rt::proc::exec_random_bytes` (reusable by S10 ASLR) reading bounded random bytes from `/scheme/rand`, and push `AT_RANDOM` (16 bytes at page-aligned offset 0 of the child's args/envs/auxv mapping) in `fexec_impl`. Fail closed when `/scheme/rand` is unavailable, with a narrow early-boot exemption for root `init` before `00_randd` registers `/scheme/rand` (omitting `AT_RANDOM` rather than fabricating a constant).
- Make `__stack_chk_guard` mutable in `.data`, copy `AT_RANDOM` into it on every start-up path (`ld.so` `stage2` via `DSO::init_self_stack_chk_guard` before `Linker::load_program` so `COPY` relocations, `GLOB_DAT` and DSO `.init_array` all see the random guard; `relibc_start_v1` for static and dynamic executables before init/constructors/main).
- Save the auxv pointer and implement bounded `getauxval` (with `<elf.h>` included from `<sys/auxv.h>`).
- Install empty `libssp.a` and `libssp_nonshared.a` beside `libdl.a`, `libpthread.a` and `librt.a` because `libc` already defines `__stack_chk_guard` and `__stack_chk_fail`.
- Propagate errors from the interpreter `fexec_impl` call in `posix_spawn` instead of panicking on `.unwrap()`, so a spawner lacking `/scheme/rand` receives `ENODEV`.

